<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cassivellaunus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cassivellaunus was a British war leader who led the resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s second invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 54 BCE. Ruling north of the Thames, he harassed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> warfare, but after the Trinovantes and other peoples went over to Caesar and his stronghold was taken, he submitted and agreed to pay tribute. He is often seen as a forerunner of the kings of the Catuvellauni.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cassivellaunus.jpg" alt="Cassivellaunus" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Miriam and Ira D. Wallach Division of Art, Prints and Photographs: Print Collection, The New York Public Library. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cassivellaunus,_New_York_Public_Library,_version2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
